// A BY-VALUE OWNER AGAINST WHAT THE CALLEE WRITES THROUGH AN EARLIER ARGUMENT, AND A SNAPSHOT THROUGH A POINTER NO NAME HOLDS (E-a and E-d's rest of DEF-410 (f); DEF-410 (b)'s other order; landing 177a).
// E-a: `wr(@s, s)` formed the address, copied the string's header, and the callee freed the bytes through the address and read them through the copy (`ea_main`, `ea_recv`: 140, the allocator's poison, on 175 and
// 176b); the other order, `wr2(s, @s)` (`ea_rev`), was BORROW-015 already. Every earlier argument is judged again against THIS snapshot alone (`rejudge_earlier`), a read-only callee legal
// (`byvalue_snapshot_earlier_ok.npk`). IT IS ONLY AS STRONG AS THE CALLEE'S SUMMARY: a write the summary misses is missed here (DEF-298's writer face, open until 179; `q2_helper`; `v_help_struct`, `v_help_lit` stay 83).
// E-d's rest: an owner read through a pointer no name holds is the same snapshot: `fs(<-(@s), K)`, `fs((<-(@h)).s, K)`, `fs(<-(is (b) : @s : @t), K)` (140). An owner CHOSEN by an operator is DEF-419's TYPE-046 now.
// DEF-410 (b)'s other order: a user call's view against an EARLIER address, `gv(@s, raw mkv(s))`, under `?!`, `relay`, a `pick` or a range too, read the bytes the callee freed through the address (83 on 176b, another string's bytes): (b) had caught only the later-argument order.
// `ea3_slice_list` is why a slice argument is judged too (140: a store through a slice element frees nothing, a `List` element's growth does); its twin on another element, `ea3_slice_list_fresh`, is over-refused until after 180.
// THE CAST (`cs_*`; E-d's rest, review A of the first build, no new number): a snapshot through a dereference under a cast, `fs((<-(@s)) => string, K)`, `fs(((<-(@h)).s) =>! string, K)` (140): the walk steps a cast on every road now.
// S1 (`s1*`; review B of the first build): a by-value value whose refs reach the snapshot's owner, `wv(W{ p: @s }, s)`, `W:w = W{ p: @s }; wv(w, s)`, `w.wm(s)`, `vw(s, w)`, through an array, an enum, an Optional, a held copy or a callee's result, or a pointer to such a holder (`wvp(@w, s)`, `w.wmp(s)`): the callee wrote through the aggregate's pointer and read the freed bytes through the snapshot (83, the next allocation's bytes). `rejudge_holder` judges it WHOLE against this call's views, either order, THE CALLEE'S SUMMARY UNREAD: a callee that writes nothing is over-refused (`s1_read_twin`, `s1_held_read_twin`, `s1x_generic`; the post-180 list).
// `we`'s body is P's over-refusal, not the cell's point: a write through a POINTER a lending arm binds lands in the pointee (`pw_write_through_binding`, the post-180 list); the call in `c_s1x_enum` is the site this file tests.
// S2 (`s2*`; review B): a slice no name holds beside a by-value owner, `ws(is (c) : arr[0...2] : arr[0...1], arr[0])`, `ws(raw ids(arr[0...2]), arr[0])` (140), asked by its targets, the summary read as the place's own road reads it.
mod:byvalue_snapshot_earlier;
